  kubectl -n nv-config-manager get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/name=nv-config-manager-render-api   # render-api Running
  kubectl -n nv-config-manager exec deploy/nv-config-manager-render-api >/dev/null 2>&1 || true

The numbered runbook (0.1 … 7.1) should be registered + enabled in the Nautobot Jobs UI.

GitRepository registration is now AUTOMATIC (gitRepo.register). The bootstrap repo is public by default, so no
secret is needed. For a PRIVATE repo, create a k8s Secret with the git token and reference it — the chart never
embeds the token in values:
  kubectl -n nv-config-manager create secret generic rafay-git --from-literal=token=<PAT>
  helm upgrade rafay-nvcm <chart> -n nv-config-manager --set gitRepo.tokenSecret.name=rafay-git

